{
  "state": "qualified_functional_increment",
  "objective_complete": false,
  "scope": "Scientific C/T/Z threshold target controls and independent histogram ROI estimation in both shared ImGui hosts; positioned write ROIs, raw histogram retention and version-three range overlays in C++/Python.",
  "behavior": "The shared OperationTargetPanel supplies captured Current/All/First/Last/Step and ROI policies. Invalid drafts disable publication while controls remain editable. Show preview plane navigates within a frozen grid. Auto estimates whole target planes or ROI members; Apply uses the same grid with its selected write ROI. To Selection retains its captured plane. Overlays display raw membership across selected XY planes including outside write ROIs. Target edits are drafts until Set/Auto/Apply.",
  "histogram": "Requested pooled histograms retain raw counts/edges including endpoint bins. Numeric-only calls preserve the original path and seven-argument C++ callable overload. Retention is admitted in working scratch; raw Mean retains its exact level while building a histogram, constants can form counts without another scan, and finite cross-zero Float64 Mean uses convex edges/scaled binning. All-Z/scientific/ROI plots display the retained target histogram. Basic single-plane calculation can still omit it. No global memory/RSS claim.",
  "state_and_records": "Nested display version three stores fully resolved, nonempty half-open T/C/Z triples with positive steps. The anchor is inside the dataset but may be outside the grid. Version-one/two forms remain supported. State membership gates XY overlays and variance/top-hat threshold reset. Z subsetting intersects/remaps the grid and drops empty intersections. Manual positioned-ROI commands use version-two records with null active-selection claims; strict source/revision binding and explicit destination rebinding remain.",
  "preferences": "Native threshold_histogram_roi and threshold_apply_roi settings are consumed and saved on successful Auto. Ranges are source-specific drafts restored from range overlays. Existing opaque-field, migration and implicit protected-write policy remains. Preference saving and display publication are separate resources, so a concurrent display conflict can refuse after preferences reached disk.",
